2.  Ensure `getSubtitles` does not crash the stream flow.

Wait, looking at `providers/vixsrc.js` again (from previous `read_file`):
```javascript
async function getSubtitles(subtitleApiUrl) {
    try {
        const response = await makeRequest(subtitleApiUrl);
        // ...
    } catch (error) {
        console.log('[Vixsrc] Subtitle fetch failed:', error.message);
        return '';
    }
}
```
It already catches errors. The issue is `makeRequest` uses `axiosInstance` which has a global `30000` ms timeout.
If `subtitleApiUrl` (`sub.wyzie.ru`) is down, it waits 30s.

I will create a specific request configuration for subtitles with a shorter timeout (e.g., 5000ms).

I'll update `providers/vixsrc.js`.

