The issue is in `getStreamsBySlug` in `providers/sflix.js`.

```javascript
async function getStreamsBySlug(id, slug, episode) {
    return await getStreamsViaApi(slug, id, 1, episode);
}
```

And `getStreamsViaApi` returns `null` or `[...]`.

```javascript
async function getStreamsViaApi(slug, subjectId, season, episode) {
    try {
        // ...
        // ... if failure ...
        return null;
    } catch (e) {
        return null;
    }
}
```

So if `getStreamsViaApi` fails (returns `null`), `getStreamsBySlug` returns `null`.
Then in `apiServer.js`:
```javascript
            fetchWithTimeout(
                (async () => {
                    if (info && info.detailPath) {
                        return sflixDirect.getStreamsBySlug(id, info.detailPath, episode);
                    }
                    // ...
                })().catch(...)
```
The async IIFE resolves to `null`.
Then:
```javascript
        const [kissStreams, sflixStreams] = await Promise.all([...]);
        let streams = [...kissStreams, ...sflixStreams];
```
Spreading `null` (`...sflixStreams`) throws "is not iterable".

I need to fix `getStreamsBySlug` to always return an array, or fix `apiServer.js` to handle `null`.
Fixing `getStreamsBySlug` to return `[]` instead of `null` is the safer, cleaner fix.

I will verify `getStreamsViaApi` implementation too. It returns `null` on line 165 and 192. It should probably return `[]` to be consistent with the "Provider Contract" (Core Mandates: "Error Handling: Providers should catch their own errors and return an empty array []").

I'll update `providers/sflix.js` to ensure array returns.

