The debug script works! It found a backdrop: `/s2qJb1FLwp1Mse9lY08JqgMp0kw.jpg`.

So why is `getHero` failing to update the item?

Let's look at `utils/hitv-api.js` again.

```javascript
            if (results && results.length > 0) {
                const match = results[0];
                if (match.backdrop_path) {
                    item.cover = `https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original${match.backdrop_path}`;
                    item.isBackdrop = true; 
                } 
                // ...
            }
```

Wait, `item` is a reference to an object in the `items` array. Modifying `item.cover` *should* modify the object in the array.

However, `browseHiTv` returns a *new object* structure.
```javascript
items: response.data.data.items.map(item => ({...}))
```

In `getHero`:
```javascript
    const res = await browseHiTv(...);
    let items = res.items || [];
    const enriched = await Promise.all(items.map(async item => {
       // ... modify item ...
       return item;
    }));
    return enriched;
```

This logic is correct. `item` is a reference.

Maybe `browseHiTv` results are being cached *before* `getHero` calls it? No, `browseHiTv` doesn't cache internally (except the massive library builder, but `getHero` calls `browseHiTv` directly with `page=1, pageSize=10`).

Wait, `utils/tmdb.js` caches `search` results.
`const key = search:${type}:${query}:${year || ''};`

If I ran the server before, maybe it cached an empty result?
But `debug-tmdb-enrich.js` worked, and it uses the *same* `utils/tmdb.js`.

Let's check the logs from the `test-hero-data.js` run earlier?
Wait, `test-hero-data.js` called the *App API directly* via `axios` in the last run (I replaced it). It did NOT call `getHero` or `browseHiTv` in the latest version.

The previous `curl` output showing the "small picture" came from the running server.

Is it possible I didn't restart the server after updating `utils/hitv-api.js` to include the enrichment logic?
I ran `lsof ... node apiServer.js` right after editing `hitv-api.js`.

Maybe `tmdb.search` is failing inside the server process for some reason (e.g. rate limit, or environment diff).

I will add logging to `getHero` in `utils/hitv-api.js` to see if it's finding matches.

Also, I noticed `utils/tmdb.js` uses `import('node-fetch')`.
`const fetch = (...args) => import('node-fetch').then(m => m.default(...args));`
This is fine in Node 18+, but if `config.tmdbApiKey` is missing (which the check script said it was "Missing" in `config`, but "Present" in `tmdbKey`), `utils/tmdb.js` relies on `config.tmdbApiKey`.

I updated `utils/tmdb.js` to use `tmdbKey` fallback.
`const apiKey = config.tmdbApiKey || getTmdbApiKey();`

I should restart the server again to be absolutely sure the new `utils/tmdb.js` and `utils/hitv-api.js` are loaded.

But before that, I'll add logs to `hitv-api.js` `getHero` to trace exactly what's happening.

